    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0646" n="574" xml:id="pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/172.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson says in view of the fact that the <hi rendition="#italic">North
                        Carolina</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Montana</hi> have proceeded so far
                    on their route to Turkey, it is hardly practicable at this late stage to recall
                    their orders. Says it is believed that the embassy will have no difficulty in
                    dispelling any misapprehension of the Turkish authorities as to the object of
                    the visit, which will be purely one of friendly courtesy to the new Government
                    now that good order has been restored and Americans are no longer in
                    jeopardy.</p>
            </div>
